From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 16:39:37 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] media: apple: avd: tests: give the recovery fixture
 the variant quirks

Commit 0c94baf620c7 ("media: apple: avd: don't reset the T6041 decoder
in recovery") made avd_pm_recover() read avd->variant->quirks for
AVD_QUIRK_NO_RECOVERY_RESET, but the host fixture in recovery-test.py
has no variant member and no quirk definition, so the test stopped
compiling ("struct avd_dev has no member named variant").

Give the fixture a struct avd_variant with the quirk bit, and check
both sides: a variant without the quirk still parks, resets and boots;
one with it returns -EIO from recovery without a reset or a boot.
The remaining cases run with no variant, as before.

With this the test passes again, and fails (SIGABRT on the new
assertion) when the quirk check in avd_pm_recover() is disabled.

Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Assisted-by: LLM
(cherry picked from commit 0d46853f530d6d0e9da816315e795a0635f1d405)
(cherry picked from commit 37961db7ac41ba3ca6511ebc0e481f4d4d4b9c92)
---
 drivers/media/platform/apple/avd/tests/recovery-test.py | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/apple/avd/tests/recovery-test.py b/drivers/media/platform/apple/avd/tests/recovery-test.py
index 66c7e0cdd8..03e78d3185 100755
--- a/drivers/media/platform/apple/avd/tests/recovery-test.py
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/apple/avd/tests/recovery-test.py
@@ -24,6 +24,7 @@ PRELUDE = r'''
 #define AVD_RECOVER_GAP_MS 20
 #define AVD_STORM_MAX 2
 #define AVD_STORM_WINDOW 60000
+#define AVD_QUIRK_NO_RECOVERY_RESET (1u << 5)
 #define msecs_to_jiffies(x) (x)
 #define jiffies_to_msecs(x) ((unsigned int)(x))
 #define time_before(a,b) ((long)((a)-(b))<0)
@@ -50,8 +51,10 @@ struct queue {
  bool (*idle)(struct avd_dev *);
  void (*resubmit)(struct avd_dev *);
 };
+struct avd_variant { unsigned int quirks; };
 struct avd_dev {
  void *dev,*domain,*empty_domain,*rstc,*compat_active;
+ const struct avd_variant *variant;
  const struct avd_backend_ops *backend;
  struct {
   bool dart_active,dma_parked,irq_enabled,hw_on;
@@ -106,7 +109,11 @@ static void init(void) {
  attached=d.domain;reset_error=boot_error=attach_error=0;
  resets=boots=attaches=detaches=shutdowns=resubmits=drains=irq_opens=irq_closes=step=0;
 }
+static const struct avd_variant plain_variant={.quirks=0};
+static const struct avd_variant no_reset_variant={.quirks=AVD_QUIRK_NO_RECOVERY_RESET};
 int main(void) {
+ init();d.variant=&plain_variant;assert(!avd_pm_recover(&d));assert(resets==1&&boots==1);
+ init();d.variant=&no_reset_variant;assert(avd_pm_recover(&d)==-EIO);assert(!resets&&!boots);
  init();assert(!avd_pm_recover(&d));assert(resets==1&&boots==1&&attaches==1&&detaches==1);
  assert(!d.pm.dma_parked&&!d.pm.irq_enabled&&attached==d.domain);
  avd_pm_enable_irq(&d);assert(irq_opens==1);
-- 
